    <briefdescription>
<para>Guarantees for concurrent model updates under churn. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><bold>Determinism:</bold> CONFLICT_RESOLVED_DETERMINISTIC <linebreak/>
 <bold>Mechanism:</bold> Last-Write-Wins with monotonic version clocks <linebreak/>
 <bold>Ordering:</bold> Version numbers form a total order; no ties</para>
<para>When two threads concurrently update the same model:<orderedlist>
<listitem><para>Both updates are stamped with unique version clocks</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Higher version number wins (LWW)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Loser either retries or receives conflict error</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Outcome is deterministic: same updates with same timing always produce same winner</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="invariant"><para>Version clocks are monotonically increasing </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="invariant"><para>No two updates have same version number </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="invariant"><para>Winner is deterministic given concurrent operation timestamps </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="invariant"><para>Loser receives explicit error (VALIDATION_INCIDENT or implicit LWW) </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
